.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.import_linter_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/

# Scratch file used to hold a DB password during local verification. Never commit.
.pwenc*
*.tmp

# Runtime logs. Rotated on disk, never in git - they contain user ids, job urls, and the shape of
# real traffic. `libs/obs` writes them here by default; LOG_DIR overrides.
logs/

# Local account credentials for the two migrated accounts. Plaintext, deliberately outside git.
# Regenerate rather than recover if lost - set_password.py overwrites.
accounts.local.txt

# Vite build output. Cloudflare Pages builds it; the repo carries the source.
web/dist/

# The cover-letter bench: prompt variants, job fixtures, the judge, and one HTML letter per
# (variant x posting). Experimental and deliberately local.
#
# Three separate reasons, any one of which is enough:
#  - It is an experiment. Prompt variants under `variants/` are candidates that have not been
#    approved, and a candidate prompt sitting in the repository next to the real one is exactly the
#    "two copies, and the enforced one is not the visible one" failure CLAUDE.md #1 is about.
#  - Its fixtures are a real person. `profile.json` and `base_cv.html` are one candidate's contact
#    details and whole career; every generated letter repeats them.
#  - Its output is regenerable and large. Megabytes per run, and a new run replaces it.
#
# `libs/scoring/coverchecks.py` is the durable half and IS tracked: it is the measurement, and the
# numbers in any prompt discussion have to be reproducible from something in the repository.
scripts/coverlab/
